== Lead ==

Collibra is a software company founded in Belgium in 2008 that develops software for data governance, data cataloging, data quality, and related enterprise data-management functions.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2017/01/18/collibra/|title=Collibra nabs $50M led by ICONIQ to fix companies' data governance|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2019/01/29/regulatory-demands-for-better-data-governance-push-collibras-valuation-above-1-billion/|title=Regulatory demands for better data governance push Collibra's valuation above $1 billion|website=TechCrunch}}</ref> The company originated as a spin-off from the Vrije Universiteit Brussel's STARLab research group.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techtransfer.research.vub.be/collibra|title=COLLIBRA|website=VUB TechTransfer}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.vub.be/en/news/from-student-spin-how-does-that-happen|title=From student to spin-off: how does that happen|website=Vrije Universiteit Brussel}}</ref> Coverage of the company has described it variously as a data governance, data management, or data intelligence vendor, reflecting product expansion and changing market vocabulary.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2017/01/18/collibra/|title=Collibra nabs $50M led by ICONIQ to fix companies' data governance|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2021/11/09/data-intelligence-company-collibra-brings-in-another-250m-to-more-than-double-its-valuation/|title=Data intelligence company Collibra brings in another $250M to more than double its valuation|website=TechCrunch}}</ref> By 2021, Collibra had reached a valuation of $5.25 billion and coverage increasingly placed it in the broader enterprise market for trusted data access, compliance, analytics enablement, and AI governance.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2021/11/09/data-intelligence-company-collibra-brings-in-another-250m-to-more-than-double-its-valuation/|title=Data intelligence company Collibra brings in another $250M to more than double its valuation|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cnbc.com/2021/11/09/collibra-doubles-valuation-as-investors-chase-next-cloud-winner.html|title=Collibra doubles valuation as investors chase next cloud winner|website=CNBC}}</ref>

== History ==

Collibra was founded in 2008 as a Belgian software company focused on helping organizations govern and use enterprise data more effectively.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2018/01/08/collibra-snags-58-m-series-d-led-by-iconiq-and-battery-ventures-to-simplify-data-governance/|title=Collibra snags $58M Series D led by Iconiq and Battery Ventures to simplify data governance|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2019/01/29/regulatory-demands-for-better-data-governance-push-collibras-valuation-above-1-billion/|title=Regulatory demands for better data governance push Collibra's valuation above $1 billion|website=TechCrunch}}</ref> VUB sources describe it as a spin-off from the university's STARLab, and identify Felix Van de Maele, Stijn Christiaens, Pieter De Leenheer, and Damien Trog as founders.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techtransfer.research.vub.be/collibra|title=COLLIBRA|website=VUB TechTransfer}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.vub.be/en/news/from-student-spin-how-does-that-happen|title=From student to spin-off: how does that happen|website=Vrije Universiteit Brussel}}</ref> Early coverage framed the company around data-governance problems inside large organizations, particularly the difficulty of finding, understanding, and controlling data spread across multiple systems.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2018/01/08/collibra-snags-58-m-series-d-led-by-iconiq-and-battery-ventures-to-simplify-data-governance/|title=Collibra snags $58M Series D led by Iconiq and Battery Ventures to simplify data governance|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2019/01/29/regulatory-demands-for-better-data-governance-push-collibras-valuation-above-1-billion/|title=Regulatory demands for better data governance push Collibra's valuation above $1 billion|website=TechCrunch}}</ref>

As regulatory scrutiny and enterprise data volumes grew, Collibra raised a succession of funding rounds that tracked its rise from a venture-backed governance vendor to a company valued above $1 billion in January 2019, $2.3 billion in April 2020, and $5.25 billion in November 2021.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2019/01/29/regulatory-demands-for-better-data-governance-push-collibras-valuation-above-1-billion/|title=Regulatory demands for better data governance push Collibra's valuation above $1 billion|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2020/04/02/collibra-nabs-another-112-5m-at-a-2-3b-valuation-for-its-big-data-management-platform/|title=Collibra nabs another $112.5M at a $2.3B valuation for its big data management platform|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2021/11/09/data-intelligence-company-collibra-brings-in-another-250m-to-more-than-double-its-valuation/|title=Data intelligence company Collibra brings in another $250M to more than double its valuation|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cnbc.com/2021/11/09/collibra-doubles-valuation-as-investors-chase-next-cloud-winner.html|title=Collibra doubles valuation as investors chase next cloud winner|website=CNBC}}</ref> Coverage of the 2020 and 2021 rounds connected that growth to governance, cataloging, data protection, and the increasing operational importance of enterprise data.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2020/04/02/collibra-nabs-another-112-5m-at-a-2-3b-valuation-for-its-big-data-management-platform/|title=Collibra nabs another $112.5M at a $2.3B valuation for its big data management platform|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2021/11/09/data-intelligence-company-collibra-brings-in-another-250m-to-more-than-double-its-valuation/|title=Data intelligence company Collibra brings in another $250M to more than double its valuation|website=TechCrunch}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cnbc.com/2021/11/09/collibra-doubles-valuation-as-investors-chase-next-cloud-winner.html|title=Collibra doubles valuation as investors chase next cloud winner|website=CNBC}}</ref>

== Products ==

Independent coverage has generally described Collibra's products as a set of enterprise tools for finding, understanding, governing, and controlling data across distributed environments.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://siliconangle.com/2021/02/03/collibra-acquires-owldq-make-enterprises-data-reliable-ai/|title=Collibra acquires OwlDQ to make enterprises' data more reliable for AI|website=SiliconANGLE}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://venturebeat.com/ai/collibra-tackles-the-shadow-ai-problem-with-new-governance-application/|title=Collibra tackles the shadow AI problem with new governance application|website=VentureBeat}}</ref> While the company's early identity was closely tied to governance and catalog functions, later coverage emphasized a broader product set that combined governance with data quality, analytics-adjacent tooling, policy controls, and AI-governance capabilities.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.techtarget.com/searchdatamanagement/news/252495815/Collibra-acquires-predictive-data-quality-vendor-OwlDQ|title=Collibra acquires predictive data quality vendor OwlDQ|website=TechTarget}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://siliconangle.com/2021/02/03/collibra-acquires-owldq-make-enterprises-data-reliable-ai/|title=Collibra acquires OwlDQ to make enterprises' data more reliable for AI|website=SiliconANGLE}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.techtarget.com/searchbusinessanalytics/news/366551315/Collibra-acquires-data-notebook-vendor-for-analytics-tools|title=Collibra acquires data notebook vendor for analytics tools|website=TechTarget}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://venturebeat.com/ai/collibra-tackles-the-shadow-ai-problem-with-new-governance-application/|title=Collibra tackles the shadow AI problem with new governance application|website=VentureBeat}}</ref>

At a high level, Collibra's product coverage in independent reporting spans data catalog and governance, data quality, analytics-oriented notebook tooling, data lineage and metadata management through acquired capabilities, and AI governance.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.techtarget.com/searchdatamanagement/news/252495815/Collibra-acquires-predictive-data-quality-vendor-OwlDQ|title=Collibra acquires predictive data quality vendor OwlDQ|website=TechTarget}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://siliconangle.com/2021/02/03/collibra-acquires-owldq-make-enterprises-data-reliable-ai/|title=Collibra acquires OwlDQ to make enterprises' data more reliable for AI|website=SiliconANGLE}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.techtarget.com/searchbusinessanalytics/news/366551315/Collibra-acquires-data-notebook-vendor-for-analytics-tools|title=Collibra acquires data notebook vendor for analytics tools|website=TechTarget}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://venturebeat.com/ai/collibra-tackles-the-shadow-ai-problem-with-new-governance-application/|title=Collibra tackles the shadow AI problem with new governance application|website=VentureBeat}}</ref>

